{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/260999-nashville-by-night-changeling-news","id":260999,"title":"Nashville By Night Changeling News","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-19T15:21:34-07:00","id":260999,"title":"Nashville By Night Changeling News","content":"The What's Up With Onyx Path panel at Nashville By Night was today. Since there were only two people in the panel starting off (and slowly grew to about five as the time went on), Rich, Eddy, and Matt decided to do the panel more as a round table discussion instead of the planned presentation.<br /> <br /> I was one of the original two, so there were more than a few Changeling: The Dreaming questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had to keep things pretty vague and hypothetical since the developer(s) hasn't been chosen yet.<br /> <br /> I asked if things were progressing on assembling a development team. Rich said he's had several pitches. He wanted to let Wraith get a bit farther in it's development process to see what Dansky does with it. Wraith's direction will probably inform the approach they'll take with Changeling since both are in the awkward position of never getting a revised core book.<br /> <br /> I mentioned that Ian Lemke has expressed interest in coming back for Changeling 20. Rich said that Changeling is big enough that it's taken on kind of a life of it's own. Whether or not Ian Lemke is the developer, he is certain that the development team will create an amazing game.<br /> <br /> The question of Kickstarted time lines came up. They were likened to trains leaving the station. They have to be in a certain order and you can't pull off one until the one before it is complete. V20 Dark Ages is next and will launch as soon as they can get a price quote from the printer so they can price the reward tiers. Wraith will probably be the next one after that. They expect to see it launch either late this year or early next. Changeling is expected to be kickstarted around mid to late next year.<br /> <br /> After a little discussion about the Mage convention books, I brought up Kithbook: Boggans. Rich said that it would be a great stretch goal for the kickstarter. I asked about the fan book for Boggans, and all three were impressed by it. I also asked about maybe nodding to it or acknowledging the fan effort in the official book in some way. They said that it was tricky. There are all kinds of legal landmines in using the material in an official book that's for sale. They did say that if it happens, they'd really like to put a special thanks at the beginning for the fans keeping the torch alive all those years.<br /> <br /> All in all, it was an amazing and fantastic panel! There was so much more discussed, but the Changeling discussion is what I remember the most clearly. I'm kind of kicking myself for not thinking to record it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}